\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The 2D pipeline. Picture plus mask first, then the random rotation/scale/colour change, then the classifier. The rotation step is exactly where the training signal gets averaged across views, which is what makes the mask work from many angles.}}{1}{}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The mask is trained on random camera angles of the whole mesh and then tested on different angles it never saw. It still works, removing the turtle prediction from every test view.}}{2}{}\protected@file@percent }
